WEBVTT

00:02.560 --> 00:05.530
In matters relating
to the world of the dead

00:05.630 --> 00:08.990
there is an institution that judges
the sins of the deceased

00:09.250 --> 00:10.790
the Ju-Oh-Cho.

00:11.630 --> 00:13.400
The Summons Section
of the Judgment Bureau

00:13.500 --> 00:17.230
comprises a group supporting
the ministry's operating functions

00:17.340 --> 00:20.170
by guiding the lost souls
that wander the mortal world.

00:20.540 --> 00:22.170
They are also known as...

00:22.410 --> 00:24.850
the Shinigami.

00:25.110 --> 00:31.780
nureta hitomi no oku

00:25.110 --> 00:31.780
Deep behind its wavering stare

00:33.490 --> 00:43.800
aoi tsuki wa shizuka ni koboreochiteyuku

00:33.490 --> 00:43.800
The pale moon quietly descends

00:33.570 --> 00:43.120
Yami no Matsuei

00:50.110 --> 00:55.980
azayaka na sekai wa

00:50.110 --> 00:55.980
The splendid world

00:58.350 --> 01:08.420
oto mo naku shizuka ni yami ni kieteyuku

00:58.350 --> 01:08.420
Disappears into the darkness without a sound

01:08.520 --> 01:16.160
byouyomi no naka kakemeguru yami no naka o

01:08.520 --> 01:16.160
Running about in the dark as time runs out

01:16.260 --> 01:22.790
soshite aratanaru toki o mukae ima

01:16.260 --> 01:22.790
A new era beckons now

01:25.510 --> 01:30.600
kizutsuita kuroi tsubasa

01:25.510 --> 01:30.600
The injured black wings

01:30.780 --> 01:37.150
tsuki no akari ni terasarete

01:30.780 --> 01:37.150
Shine in the moonlight

01:37.750 --> 01:41.950
utsukushiku maiagare

01:37.750 --> 01:41.950
Rising upward in a beautiful dance

01:42.090 --> 01:47.290
shinku no kuchizuke ga ima

01:42.090 --> 01:47.290
The crimson kiss

01:47.400 --> 01:54.230
kokoro no oku ni nagarekomu

01:47.400 --> 01:54.230
Flows deeply into the soul

01:54.400 --> 02:00.200
soshite yume no naka e

01:54.400 --> 02:00.200
Penetrating into one's dreams

02:25.680 --> 02:28.850
Orlando Hill

02:56.800 --> 03:01.800
Episode 1: Nagasaki Arc, Part 1

03:30.870 --> 03:33.040
Summoning Department

03:36.070 --> 03:39.870
This is the victim from the latest
serial killings in Nagasaki.

03:39.970 --> 03:42.170
How horrible.

03:42.280 --> 03:45.710
All of the victims have puncture wounds
from what appears to be fangs...

03:45.810 --> 03:49.210
and they have lost virtually
all of their blood.

03:49.650 --> 03:51.740
Like from a vampire.

03:51.990 --> 03:54.220
Seems like a supernatural crime.

03:54.320 --> 03:58.690
It's precisely because this case cannot
be explained that we got the call.

03:58.790 --> 04:00.230
That's right.

04:00.330 --> 04:02.820
Tsuzuki, I want you to head
to Nagasaki right... huh?

04:05.620 --> 04:07.580
Conference Room

04:06.330 --> 04:07.530
Tsuzuki!

04:10.540 --> 04:13.250
Tsuzuki   Stakeout at Earth!

04:11.170 --> 04:12.970
"Stakeout at Earth"?

04:19.650 --> 04:21.620
She's late.

04:21.670 --> 04:23.880
Ladies' Day Half Price Special!

04:21.670 --> 04:23.880
Time for something sweet.

04:22.320 --> 04:24.440
I hope they haven't run out.

04:24.550 --> 04:26.180
Here. Sorry to keep you waiting.

04:26.920 --> 04:28.820
All right!

04:29.560 --> 04:32.460
I just love the smell
of this caramel cream.

04:32.560 --> 04:34.050
Thanks, Wakaba-chan!

04:34.160 --> 04:37.260
Tsuzuki-chan, you sure have
a sweet tooth, don't you?

04:38.230 --> 04:41.630
I always make sure I have a dessert
after all three meals.

04:42.970 --> 04:46.300
It's already this late?
Your lunch break's long over!

04:47.280 --> 04:50.400
So, this is the cinnamon roll
that compelled you

04:50.510 --> 04:53.140
to skip an investigation meeting?

04:53.250 --> 04:54.510
It looks pretty good.

04:54.620 --> 04:56.550
Could I please have it back, Boss?

04:56.650 --> 04:57.580
Here.

04:58.050 --> 04:59.110
Watari!

04:59.220 --> 05:00.520
It sure smells good. Catch!

05:00.720 --> 05:01.380
Gushoushin...

05:01.490 --> 05:03.720
Looks delicious! Catch!

05:05.590 --> 05:07.220
Tatsumi...

05:08.000 --> 05:11.360
It's not nice to tease Tsuzuki-san so much.

05:11.470 --> 05:12.870
Ta-Tatsumi!

05:12.970 --> 05:13.590
Thank...

05:13.700 --> 05:16.030
Well, let's all share this.

05:20.270 --> 05:22.940
Just a tiny piece left...

05:25.610 --> 05:27.510
Thank you.

05:27.620 --> 05:30.280
All right.
Let's get serious now.

05:30.390 --> 05:32.350
Tsuzuki, I want you to fly
to Nagasaki right away.

05:32.450 --> 05:33.320
Huh?

05:33.690 --> 05:36.660
If you don't like that,
I can fire you right now.

05:36.760 --> 05:39.520
You're just an ordinary worker,
with a mere 70 years of service.

05:40.360 --> 05:42.090
I'd be happy to go, of course!

05:42.960 --> 05:43.590
Good grief...

05:43.700 --> 05:46.460
And, what am I supposed
to look into, Boss?

05:46.570 --> 05:50.370
There's one who hasn't died,
despite reaching the natural life span.

05:50.470 --> 05:51.900
Determining the causes

05:52.010 --> 05:54.030
and capturing those lost souls

05:54.140 --> 05:57.080
is the work of the Summons Section
of the Judgment Bureau.

05:57.180 --> 06:02.010
Lately, there've been names
that have remained on the register.

06:02.120 --> 06:05.850
Don't we check the number
of total deaths per day here?

06:05.950 --> 06:07.650
Exactly.

06:08.560 --> 06:12.050
The stipulations as determined
at the Hall of Candles

06:12.160 --> 06:15.490
require one to pass into
the netherworld when one dies.

06:16.160 --> 06:18.690
However, the Ju-Oh-Cho is only able to

06:18.800 --> 06:21.170
account for those who have
died of mysterious circumstances.

06:21.540 --> 06:24.530
As for accidents or murders
involving third parties

06:24.640 --> 06:27.400
we don't know about it until it's
automatically noted in the register.

06:28.610 --> 06:32.840
In other words, more are dying
of mysterious circumstances?

06:32.950 --> 06:34.640
That's right.

06:34.750 --> 06:38.910
And by the way Tsuzuki, all in
your district of Nagasaki.

06:39.190 --> 06:41.590
I understand.
Oh, but what about a partner?

06:41.690 --> 06:43.990
Right. We've finally
found one for you.

06:44.090 --> 06:46.960
I'll have him meet up with you later,
so go to Nagasaki first.

06:47.060 --> 06:49.660
Until then, I'll send Gushoushin with you.

06:49.760 --> 06:51.130
Looking forward to it.

06:51.230 --> 06:53.460
He'll give you all the details.

06:53.700 --> 06:54.570
Hang on, Tsuzuki.

06:54.670 --> 06:55.600
Take this.

06:55.970 --> 06:57.730
A send-off gift?!

06:57.840 --> 07:00.070
They've got good sweet cakes
in Nagasaki, right?

07:00.170 --> 07:01.610
Bring some back for me.

07:03.080 --> 07:05.170
Don't forget this, too.

07:03.380 --> 07:04.840
Allowance book
for good little boys

07:05.380 --> 07:07.750
I won't accept wasteful expenditures.

07:07.850 --> 07:10.480
I want you to keep your daily
meal expenses down to 3,000 yen.

07:10.590 --> 07:12.490
How can I afford dessert...

07:12.590 --> 07:14.680
What's decided is decided.

07:16.520 --> 07:17.650
Have a good trip.

07:17.760 --> 07:20.160
Don't eat too much.

07:25.930 --> 07:27.490
Welcome.

07:27.600 --> 07:28.730
Thank you.

07:34.410 --> 07:36.570
This fruity aroma...

07:36.680 --> 07:40.410
Is this first flush Darjeeling,
Watson?

07:40.520 --> 07:43.420
That's right, Count.

07:43.820 --> 07:44.680
I see...

07:46.220 --> 07:48.850
I hope it goes well this time.

07:48.960 --> 07:50.360
Me too.

07:50.460 --> 07:53.220
People are different
every time you see them.

07:53.430 --> 07:58.020
Yes. That goes for Tsuzuki, and him...

08:00.100 --> 08:02.190
It's a weird case, I tell ya.

08:02.300 --> 08:05.240
The fang marks in the neck

08:05.340 --> 08:07.270
and the total loss of blood.

08:07.780 --> 08:11.940
This case is now called
the "Vampire Case."

08:12.950 --> 08:14.710
Vampire, huh?

08:15.150 --> 08:19.110
Well, how about we fortify
ourselves with a meal?

08:20.090 --> 08:23.350
Come on! I wish you'd take things
more seriously, Tsuzuki-san!

08:26.730 --> 08:27.720
Are you all right?!

08:33.870 --> 08:34.960
Lipstick?

08:35.770 --> 08:37.290
Tsuzuki-san!

08:40.680 --> 08:42.200
It was that girl!

08:44.110 --> 08:45.810
<i>That wasn't lipstick!</i>

08:46.680 --> 08:48.340
<i>It's the victim's blood!</i>

08:50.080 --> 08:51.810
Tsuzuki-san!

09:36.100 --> 09:39.190
Uh, did you see a girl...?

09:48.410 --> 09:50.500
How embarrassing this is.

09:50.610 --> 09:52.370
Oh, uh, don't worry...

09:52.480 --> 09:53.640
Is there something...?

09:53.750 --> 09:58.380
Oh, uh... Did you see a girl
come in here?

09:58.490 --> 09:59.680
With long hair?

09:59.790 --> 10:01.850
No. No one.

10:02.020 --> 10:04.650
Oh, I see. Excuse me.

10:30.150 --> 10:32.310
Where is she?
Where'd she go?

10:38.690 --> 10:39.790
Don't move.

10:54.440 --> 10:58.990
Yami no Matsuei

11:04.190 --> 11:06.280
I think you've got
the wrong person.

11:06.620 --> 11:09.780
Put your hands up,
and slowly turn around.

11:13.630 --> 11:15.600
What? You're just a kid!

11:15.700 --> 11:20.860
Getting held up by a kid says a lot
about your carelessness.

11:21.240 --> 11:24.330
What the...?! How did he know
my exact thought?!

11:24.570 --> 11:28.170
I don't mess around
with crucifixes and garlic.

11:28.280 --> 11:31.040
I'll play it straight
and send a bullet into your heart.

11:31.150 --> 11:32.370
Huh? Vampire-san?

11:32.480 --> 11:34.240
Vampire?! Who?!

11:34.350 --> 11:36.750
Don't play dumb with me.
I've been watching you

11:36.850 --> 11:39.980
lurking around here,
looking suspicious.

11:40.520 --> 11:43.150
<i>Who on earth is this guy?</i>

11:44.160 --> 11:46.250
<i>I can't jump in my human form.</i>

11:46.360 --> 11:49.490
<i>And it's too dangerous
to use any spells with people around.</i>

11:49.830 --> 11:51.800
This is the end. Give it up.

11:53.600 --> 11:55.570
Hold it!

11:56.070 --> 11:58.700
What are you trying to do, anyway?!

11:58.810 --> 12:02.170
No! He's the one
who's holding me up!

12:02.280 --> 12:03.680
Shut up, Vampire.

12:03.780 --> 12:05.750
You've got the wrong guy!

12:07.350 --> 12:11.410
He's the one!
This is your new partner, Tsuzuki-san!

12:11.520 --> 12:12.180
Huh?

12:12.750 --> 12:15.650
Now, let's celebrate
new acquaintances!

12:15.760 --> 12:17.880
Cheers!

12:19.760 --> 12:21.920
Tsuzuki-san, how about a smile?

12:22.030 --> 12:25.490
Well, I'm Tsuzuki.
In charge of Kyushu.

12:26.000 --> 12:27.970
I'm Kurosaki Hisoka.

12:30.000 --> 12:32.500
<i>Wh-What's this attitude
he's giving me?</i>

12:32.610 --> 12:35.970
Boss Konoe personally decided
to use him

12:36.080 --> 12:39.070
because apparently
his spiritual powers are quite strong.

12:39.180 --> 12:41.580
That's why you were able
to read my mind?

12:41.680 --> 12:43.740
By the way, how old are you?

12:43.850 --> 12:44.550
Sixteen.

12:44.650 --> 12:45.580
Sixteen?

12:45.690 --> 12:48.450
You died awfully young.
Car accident?

12:48.560 --> 12:49.750
T-Tsuzuki-san...!

12:49.860 --> 12:53.020
Died of illness.
An incurable illness.

12:54.960 --> 12:56.950
Oh. Sorry...

12:57.060 --> 13:00.630
Don't worry.
But I have a question for you.

13:02.270 --> 13:05.930
You're in the top career track
at the Judgment Bureau, right?

13:06.040 --> 13:09.600
So, why would an elite guy
like you be a Shinigami?

13:09.710 --> 13:11.970
Elite? Me?

13:15.150 --> 13:17.170
Tsuzuki-san is an elite?!

13:17.280 --> 13:18.910
This man is famous
for his slack attitude

13:19.020 --> 13:21.950
and is called "The Sugar Glutton
of Hades" by his bosses!

13:22.390 --> 13:24.120
But, Boss Konoe said...

13:24.330 --> 13:28.130
I see. You really don't know, do you?
How nice...

13:28.230 --> 13:30.560
Wh-What do you mean by that?

13:30.660 --> 13:34.290
The rule is that Shinigami
are to work in pairs.

13:34.400 --> 13:38.530
But nobody ever wants to partner
with Tsuzuki-san.

13:39.170 --> 13:40.370
You've got to be kidding!

13:40.470 --> 13:43.440
No way I'm going to be fooled
into working with some idiot!

13:43.540 --> 13:45.010
I'm getting off here!

13:45.850 --> 13:47.840
Hey, this is good.

13:47.950 --> 13:50.420
Stop eating and listen
to what I'm saying!

13:56.120 --> 13:57.610
You ate my dumpling...

13:57.730 --> 14:00.160
Huh? I thought you didn't want it.

14:06.130 --> 14:07.570
Now we're even!

14:08.240 --> 14:10.430
You don't want me
to hold a grudge over food.

14:10.540 --> 14:12.940
Especially in regard to this!

14:24.550 --> 14:25.850
It's mine!

14:28.110 --> 14:28.740
Extra Spicy

14:29.760 --> 14:31.520
It's hot!

14:33.460 --> 14:34.950
Hey, that's my...!

14:40.940 --> 14:41.960
Oh, boy...

14:42.970 --> 14:45.960
Come on! Lay him down there
and give him some water!

14:46.070 --> 14:47.230
All right. All right.

14:47.940 --> 14:50.380
But why do I have to do this
in the first place?

14:50.480 --> 14:54.070
It's because you got
into a stupid fight with a kid.

14:54.180 --> 14:56.710
He can be cute
if he keeps his mouth shut.

14:56.820 --> 14:59.450
A Shinigami at the age of sixteen...

14:59.550 --> 15:02.020
It's kind of sad, isn't it?

15:09.530 --> 15:12.400
I'm sure this guy's got his reasons.

15:12.500 --> 15:17.230
Otherwise, he wouldn't be doing
dirty work like being a Shinigami.

15:25.310 --> 15:27.970
Maybe I looked a bit childish.

15:28.080 --> 15:29.740
Tsuzuki-san...

15:29.950 --> 15:32.210
Tsuzuki, you stupid idiot !

15:32.320 --> 15:35.450
Don't think you're going
to get away with this.

15:36.590 --> 15:39.460
I take back what I said!

15:42.530 --> 15:43.930
Isn't that beautiful?

15:44.030 --> 15:45.860
Is it some kind of festival?

15:45.970 --> 15:48.430
Opening night
for the Nagasaki Singing Festival.

15:48.540 --> 15:51.270
I'm pretty sure it's on TV.

15:51.870 --> 15:54.530
<i>The opening night
of the Nagasaki Singing Festival.</i>

15:54.640 --> 15:56.580
<i>We're watching the fireworks go off.</i>

15:56.680 --> 16:01.050
<i>And, right here, I've got with me
the popular singer from Hong Kong</i>

16:01.150 --> 16:03.840
<i>Miss Maria Wong!</i>

16:05.020 --> 16:05.990
<i>Good evening.</i>

16:06.090 --> 16:08.380
Isn't she beautiful?!

16:16.030 --> 16:17.590
That woman...!

16:18.200 --> 16:19.890
What's the matter?

16:20.430 --> 16:23.600
Gushoushin, could you
look into something for me?

16:27.570 --> 16:29.870
What a beautiful morning!

16:31.250 --> 16:35.110
What's up? You don't look
too good this morning, kid.

16:35.220 --> 16:37.380
Don't call me "kid"!

16:37.720 --> 16:40.620
I guess you're still
a bit young to be drinking.

16:40.720 --> 16:41.850
Just shut up!

16:45.260 --> 16:46.620
That's cold.

16:47.030 --> 16:48.690
It'll refresh you.

16:50.360 --> 16:52.030
Tsuzuki...

16:52.130 --> 16:56.470
That was the first time
you called me by my name.

17:01.110 --> 17:02.470
Hey!

17:06.350 --> 17:10.650
It's not like I've accepted you
as my partner.

17:11.890 --> 17:13.580
I don't mind.

17:18.630 --> 17:20.720
Well, I guess we'll
start our investigation.

17:20.830 --> 17:22.630
At a TV studio?

17:22.730 --> 17:26.790
A vampire might be here.
Right, Gushoushin?

17:26.900 --> 17:29.660
Yes, just as you expected, Tsuzuki-san...

17:29.770 --> 17:34.430
The vampire incidents and the arrival
of Maria Wong coincide!

17:34.540 --> 17:38.000
So, you think she's the culprit
behind the vampire case?

17:38.110 --> 17:39.940
That's what we're going to find out.

17:40.050 --> 17:42.410
When did you figure all that out?

17:43.150 --> 17:47.140
While you took over my bed.

17:48.760 --> 17:50.380
Well, I'll be on my way.

17:50.490 --> 17:52.620
Now that you've got your partner

17:52.730 --> 17:55.390
I can go back
to my job at the library.

17:55.500 --> 17:58.360
Hisoka-san, I leave Tsuzuki-san in your hands.

17:58.470 --> 17:59.360
Hey, hey!

17:59.470 --> 18:03.030
I'm looking forward
to your souvenirs!

18:06.170 --> 18:07.440
Let's go.

18:08.010 --> 18:08.840
Sure.

18:17.260 --> 18:17.550
Maria Wong

18:18.010 --> 18:22.100
Maria Wong

18:20.350 --> 18:22.220
- What do you think?
- I don't sense anything.

18:27.930 --> 18:30.760
Maria?! Where are you, Maria?!

18:32.100 --> 18:34.160
What are you people doing there?

18:34.270 --> 18:35.860
Well, uh...

18:38.210 --> 18:39.570
I just wanted to get her autograph.

18:39.670 --> 18:40.440
This way!

18:40.540 --> 18:41.630
H-Hey!

18:42.680 --> 18:45.300
You know where she is?

18:45.680 --> 18:48.440
I am able to tell from her
spiritual trace residue in the room!

18:48.550 --> 18:50.210
Right.

19:05.070 --> 19:06.970
You're not allowed in here.

19:07.500 --> 19:09.370
M-Maria Wong?

19:13.170 --> 19:13.970
Uh...!

19:23.920 --> 19:24.850
Get away from her!

19:25.950 --> 19:27.350
Wh-What's this...?!

19:34.560 --> 19:35.820
Maria!

19:41.000 --> 19:41.970
A beast!

19:42.070 --> 19:43.560
A dragon!

19:43.670 --> 19:45.300
Stay back!

19:45.410 --> 19:46.370
This is not for kids.

19:46.470 --> 19:47.770
Don't call me "kid"!

19:55.680 --> 19:56.980
Tsuzuki...

20:01.990 --> 20:04.220
Hisoka, go and help him!

20:12.600 --> 20:14.790
I bow to thee and beseech you.

20:14.900 --> 20:17.060
The Twelve Gods that protect me.

20:17.170 --> 20:19.260
Appear before me!

20:20.110 --> 20:22.040
Come out! Suzaku!

20:43.760 --> 20:45.060
Explode!

21:04.350 --> 21:06.440
Maria Wong is dead?

21:06.920 --> 21:10.080
Yeah. She's been on the register
for two months.

21:10.190 --> 21:12.920
According to information
from China, it was suicide.

21:14.190 --> 21:16.750
Then, what we saw was...

21:26.440 --> 21:28.700
Maria, you're a good girl.

21:28.810 --> 21:33.040
There's nothing to worry about
as long as you do as I say.

21:33.510 --> 21:36.070
As long as you do as I say.

21:39.960 --> 21:43.010
Next Episode

21:43.160 --> 21:45.420
In the serial murders
that took place in Nagasaki

21:45.530 --> 21:48.980
the culprit turns out
to be a vampire, Maria Wong.

21:49.430 --> 21:52.560
Who on earth is manipulating her?

21:54.430 --> 21:56.430
We can't work on an empty stomach.

21:56.540 --> 21:58.130
Hisoka, let's get something to eat.

21:58.240 --> 21:59.870
We just ate!

22:00.340 --> 22:09.910
Episode 2 Nagasaki Arc, Part 2

22:00.340 --> 22:04.250
Next time on Yami no Matsuei:
The Nagasaki Arc, Part 2.

22:05.410 --> 22:08.580
Those who live in the darkness wander aimlessly.

22:18.230 --> 22:21.590
arumikan no marui en o mashikaku ni orinagara

22:18.230 --> 22:21.590
As I square the round edges on the drink

22:21.700 --> 22:24.630
kimi o matsu machikado sa

22:21.700 --> 22:24.630
I wait for you on the street corner

22:24.730 --> 22:28.220
nakami no ekitai wa mou nurukute nomenai kedo

22:24.730 --> 22:28.220
The liquid inside is warm and I can't drink it anymore

22:28.340 --> 22:30.930
shikatanaku motsu ore sa

22:28.340 --> 22:30.930
But what can I do but hold onto to it?

22:31.040 --> 22:38.270
yami no naka de ore o utsusu
garasu keesu ni kazarareta

22:31.040 --> 22:38.270
In the glass case reflecting me in the darkness

22:38.380 --> 22:45.010
ningyou ga sakki kara kowai
kao de ore o miteru

22:38.380 --> 22:45.010
There is a doll that has been scowling at me

22:58.470 --> 23:04.890
ore no fuku kuchibue wa wari
to akarui uta de

22:58.470 --> 23:04.890
The tune I whistle is a bright and cheerful one

